    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen using multicursors by putting some cursors on some nodes (let's say headings of a markdown), `{visual}an` only expands the selection where the main cursor is present and other cursors' selection isn't updated\n\nDoing any change command works fine like `can` apart from it not showing the changes in realtime on other cursors (updates after going back to normal mode)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nEdit any markdown file\n```\nnvim --clean\n:e README.md\n```\nAdd cursors on headings with `Q` in normal mode and try expanding selection `van`\n\nOnly the heading under main cursor has selection expansion.\n\n\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe selection should expand/contract on nodes at each cursor position\n\n\n0.13.0 commit \n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1531+g48864161cd\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNA, vim doesn't have multicursors\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narchlinux 7.1.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nInstalled nightly version using bob",
